  "updated_at": "2026-11-10T15:34:57Z",
  "body": "Good point to bring up, @SkyZeroZx — just to clarify, the limitation in PR #70227 only applies to **outgoing `POST` requests with `Blob`/`FormData` request bodies** (as noted under `includePostRequests` in `ssr.md`). For a `GET` request with `responseType: 'blob'` (or `httpResource.blob()`), there is no `Blob` in the request—the cache key is derived synchronously from the URL, method, and params as usual. #71917 is strictly about serializing the **response** `Blob` in `transferCacheInterceptorFn` / `toBase64()`.\n\nBecause #70227 only touches request-side cache keys in `makeCacheKey()` and skips `Blob`/`FormData` request payloads, fixing response-side `Blob` caching here won't conflict with #70227 (and I'll make sure to rebase if #70227 lands first).\n\n@JeanMeche Could you please assign #71917 to me? I already have a working fix and regression tests ready locally (preserving `Blob` bytes and `type` via `body.arrayBuffer()` during `ngServerMode`) and would like to open the PR for it once you're happy with the approach.",
